-- title:
--   Deuring surjectivity: every maximal order is a supersingular endomorphism ring
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field, $q'$ a prime with $\kappa$ of characteristic $q'$, equipped with a $\mathbb{Z}/q'$-algebra structure under which $\kappa$ is algebraic over $\mathbb{Z}/q'$. Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ satisfy `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q'`, i.e. $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of the ring of integers of $\mathbb{Q}$ the base change $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division ring (every nonzero element is a unit) exactly when $q'$ lies in $v$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order: it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, it is finitely generated, and every order containing it equals it. Then there exist a Weierstrass curve $X_0$ over $\kappa$ and a proof that $X_0$ is elliptic such that the only point $P$ of the affine model of $X_0$ with $q'\cdot P=0$ is $P=0$, together with a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`WeierstrassCurve.rationalEndSubring κ X₀`](def/WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd.html#L32) — the subring of additive endomorphisms of the points of the base change of $X_0$ generated by those endomorphisms that are zero or rationally represented — into $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is injective and whose range is exactly $\Lambda$ as a subset.
--
--   This is the surjective, or onto, half of Deuring's correspondence: not merely that the endomorphism ring of a supersingular elliptic curve in characteristic $q'$ is a maximal order in the definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $q'$ and $\infty$, but that every prescribed maximal order $\Lambda$ is realised, which matters because maximal orders of a definite quaternion algebra need not be conjugate. It is used by the Čerednik–Drinfeld constructions that transport a fixed maximal order to a quaternionic group law and to the identification of class sets with supersingular places compatibly with degeneracy and Hecke operators.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_supersingular_rationalEndSubring_range_eq_of_isMaximalOrder.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_QuaternionAlgebra_EichlerOrder
import Definitions.Def_WeierstrassCurve_RationalEnd

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
